      "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/e445a64d7e90c038479e65e10547ce00efa7460c",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "2b74d0a2cfd69ff3dea30e77fece6b32b30555f4",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/trees/2b74d0a2cfd69ff3dea30e77fece6b32b30555f4"
      },
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree 2b74d0a2cfd69ff3dea30e77fece6b32b30555f4\nparent 6d994c29f1c6a4b50dcc0e7be76a4f2e9240640a\nauthor Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792799959 +0200\ncommitter Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792874108 +0200\n\ntorcontrol: Only use a SOCKS listener on the Tor control host\n\nThe reply to GETINFO net/listeners/socks is used as the proxy for onion\naddresses. Whoever answers on the control port can name any address,\nand all onion connections then go through it.\n\nOnly accept a listener on the host that runs the control port: a\nloopback address if the control port is on loopback, otherwise the\naddress the control port was reached at. Log a warning for each other\nlistener, including a unix socket. This keeps working a remote Tor\nreached with -torcontrol, which a loopback-only rule would break.\n\nIf no listener is accepted, keep the onion proxy that is already set,\nsuch as the one from -proxy, instead of replacing it with 127.0.0.1:9050.\nWithout one, the default 127.0.0.1:9050 is still used. A listener on\n127.0.0.1 is still preferred over other accepted ones.\n",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQRJ5SMZs3eEinN+Lb4iedqLwmlHIAUCat0WfBsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQInnai8JpRyCJnwEAgLkIReCtezIUtORDkExv\n6UV+21cP0/gD1nnUSHBxziIA/0qRsvO5z5FJds++bZDTKy3zwRI6SyYaRWgyIgfd\ntmoO\n=AsMl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----"
      },
